## Decisions

### Does this schema fit the classroom deck import?

You asked to review the data model before building the importer, then review homepage mockups before UI implementation. I recommend reusing the document tables and adding three classroom fields.

```diagram
row
  classroom "GROUP · classroom" "new: update → current DOCUMENT" "new: update_image → PNG · update_url → slide" blue
row
  audience "DOCUMENT_GROUP" "sent_to → classroom + classroom parents" green
  current "DOCUMENT · current deck" "kind=file · url=canonical deck URL" "content → full Markdown" blue
  png "CONTENT · newest slide" "image/png · original exported bytes" green
row
  old "DOCUMENT · earlier deck" "same canonical URL · content retained" plain
  markdown "CONTENT · deck text" "text/markdown · all slides and links" green
classroom -> current "update"
classroom -> png "update_image"
audience -> classroom "group"
audience -> current "document"
old -> current "superseded_by"
current -> markdown "content"
```

`GROUP` holds classrooms. Proposed fields: `update` references the current deck document; `update_image` references the newest-slide PNG bytes; `update_url` opens that captured slide. `DOCUMENT` holds each deck version, with `kind=file` meaning a shared file, `url` holding its canonical Google Slides address, and `content` referencing its Markdown bytes. `CONTENT` stores deduplicated bytes. `DOCUMENT_GROUP` associates a document with its audiences; `sent_to` currently grants access to that group's members and managers. `superseded_by` points an older document at its whole-document replacement.

Real input: the exported **Hummingbirds (K) Updates 2026-2027** deck contains 43 slides. Its canonical [deck URL](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1BaHd4hKaF152gTCsGUvWpMsewxbzeSfFItRMOlH0i1A/edit) identifies the deck; the newest image is slide 1.

- (*) Approve this schema
  Hummingbirds gets a current-document reference, its native PNG reference, and the exported direct slide link. The document holds all 43 slides as Markdown and is sent to Hummingbirds and Hummingbirds Parents, letting their members and managers read it through Ask. The PNG follows the same audience. Changed Markdown at the same deck URL produces a replacement document and retains the earlier text; identical Markdown creates no version. A changed PNG alone updates the classroom image. I recommend this because it uses the existing storage, audience and replacement mechanisms. Next I implement the importer and prepare homepage mockups for separate review.
